[{:db/id "q-36720/selection/987f9538a46fe36f0b5620c053da1a956067965f6f79ea549700d3fda7844d1b" :answer/id #uuid "c784541e-c62f-5d95-9a7e-66e2f4a91957" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36720/selection/443bd8bb4d0d1697a9600df62b3ad517827a2d6ff769991c91f9bc651eac1877" :answer/id #uuid "9ca728f2-222f-5999-ae9e-98fcc6a6a393" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36720/selection/2fcf1e1cc9dda8dec15fde59c161143b6e830e3599d04a02b7fc85571540ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a193b055-26f2-5fa7-81ea-f9d494715f67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36720/selection/3c4b0edee4070ab4f26e90b2ac22624ccd8a08138442236e463e657cc7f41681" :answer/id #uuid "938764f7-b8ee-58fa-a2b2-c02af0672079" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36720/selection/3782dc5fd4d806c5aec0fd85d6556244672b1f181b1651fef67d05db7e105125" :answer/id #uuid "c5dcc2c8-07db-5c23-8ff7-34f4c000ffa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36720/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "32251415-ec0f-5079-bdb4-a2aedb7c2af3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36720/selection/3c4b0edee4070ab4f26e90b2ac22624ccd8a08138442236e463e657cc7f41681" :answer-field/choices ["q-36720/selection/987f9538a46fe36f0b5620c053da1a956067965f6f79ea549700d3fda7844d1b" "q-36720/selection/443bd8bb4d0d1697a9600df62b3ad517827a2d6ff769991c91f9bc651eac1877" "q-36720/selection/2fcf1e1cc9dda8dec15fde59c161143b6e830e3599d04a02b7fc85571540ed03" "q-36720/selection/3c4b0edee4070ab4f26e90b2ac22624ccd8a08138442236e463e657cc7f41681" "q-36720/selection/3782dc5fd4d806c5aec0fd85d6556244672b1f181b1651fef67d05db7e105125"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36720" :question/id #uuid "4da9acce-fbe4-5910-b619-3be32acf4b46" :question/math-academy-id "q-36720" :question/problem "Find the limit at $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}6x+1\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -4{log}_{2}⁡x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the left, we have $x<\\frac{1}{2},$ so we use the expression $f(x)=6x+1.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {(1/2)}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(1/2)}^{-}}(6x+1) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow,  approaching from the right, we have $x>\\frac{1}{2},$ so we use the expression $f(x)=-4{log}_{2}⁡x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {(1/2)}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(1/2)}^{+}}-4{log}_{2}⁡x \\\\  & =-4{log}_{2}⁡\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-4{log}_{2}⁡{2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-4(-1){log}_{2}⁡2 \\\\  & =-4(-1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left- and right-sided limits are equal to $4,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-36720/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0995bfd4-20b1-5f12-9d1d-fcb180a6291e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36720"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-99959/selection/048ad321e5bba6dad48726b952c5e314b0c237eac655a0b5356dc0433ae2bd7b" :answer/id #uuid "6c05a92f-9232-5a57-8d62-60cd2794ef0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99959/selection/b001cd078c3e5323aecef64b0e88329691573ab7e25717a9c3276c434b0a1b0a" :answer/id #uuid "8b68b77b-2add-5ab1-84b2-acee5015d68a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99959/selection/edfaaf1819787dffec492dc9f6ce815d6f632212e50b83b2b84d388287d4b33c" :answer/id #uuid "9f84b58c-2a20-539e-9ad3-de7114007287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99959/selection/9f33aebbf11dd31ace2f174b42da1f6729ce8d816b931aa518df01723a326081" :answer/id #uuid "5061f948-f802-5f85-bda6-c0b634f3fbef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99959/selection/69b1aa67aa2eb302f08a7d8822d3bf5c2df21d05787213f7316d456cf0b652be" :answer/id #uuid "2639cb3c-6fa9-56a9-8800-dfade5e09150" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99959/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "81c8b20a-17e9-51f7-9df8-a61ec673f47c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-99959/selection/9f33aebbf11dd31ace2f174b42da1f6729ce8d816b931aa518df01723a326081" :answer-field/choices ["q-99959/selection/048ad321e5bba6dad48726b952c5e314b0c237eac655a0b5356dc0433ae2bd7b" "q-99959/selection/b001cd078c3e5323aecef64b0e88329691573ab7e25717a9c3276c434b0a1b0a" "q-99959/selection/edfaaf1819787dffec492dc9f6ce815d6f632212e50b83b2b84d388287d4b33c" "q-99959/selection/9f33aebbf11dd31ace2f174b42da1f6729ce8d816b931aa518df01723a326081" "q-99959/selection/69b1aa67aa2eb302f08a7d8822d3bf5c2df21d05787213f7316d456cf0b652be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-99959" :question/id #uuid "440fe138-4ebc-525f-9943-9ea9999a6962" :question/math-academy-id "q-99959" :question/problem "Find the limit at $x=-1$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt[3]{x}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<-1 \\\\ -2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x=-1 \\\\ x+2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the left, we have $x<-1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=-\\sqrt[3]{x}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -{1}^{-}}-\\sqrt[3]{x} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt[3]{-1} \\\\  & =-(-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApproaching from the right, we have $x>-1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=x+2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}(x+2) \\\\  & =-1+2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left- and right-sided limits are equal to $1,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-99959/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0995bfd4-20b1-5f12-9d1d-fcb180a6291e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99959"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339732/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "644df85c-5f72-56e0-9df5-abfdebd72356" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339732/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "045fffb4-9e06-586d-a853-b10378d20892" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339732/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fd6a0b7-1b27-5274-96ab-a1926974f446" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339732/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-339732/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-339732/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339732/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "419fa797-bf64-5c85-911b-3a89ca338639" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339732/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5248d949-86fa-568c-b5a4-a781e1aca325" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339732/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-339732/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339732" :question/id #uuid "d94bc837-284e-5745-a87c-0eafdefad454" :question/math-academy-id "q-339732" :question/problem "Find the left- and right-sided limits at $x=-2$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x} & \\text{ for }\\,x<-2 \\\\ {e}^{2+x}+3 & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge -2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}},$\\,$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}f(x)=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the left, we have $x<-2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-6x} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-6(-2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+12} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApproaching from the right, we have $x\\ge -2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)={e}^{2+x}+3.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}{e}^{2+x}+3 \\\\  & ={e}^{2+(-2)}+3 \\\\  & ={e}^{0}+3 \\\\  & =1+3 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}f(x)=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339732/field-1" "q-339732/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0995bfd4-20b1-5f12-9d1d-fcb180a6291e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339732"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-36689/selection/ddedad0302f892b63bf1e984a158163f154d4d6538ed080f2a33dd117942102a" :answer/id #uuid "a48c4ec8-a20d-5ff2-afdb-ec2dd23b8b3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x)=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36689/selection/8f1878b9a3e2c6e1f6d2557dc5bc5895e8a9cdd0aa2e6ee51aee1e1dcbcc153a" :answer/id #uuid "a6d60a80-1a19-5e81-b835-7075f2bcf3d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)=1,\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x)=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36689/selection/6e204d9b0a5fef6e7dd8e47841a025509ba9d4cebc253b0f618e32391fae7411" :answer/id #uuid "2c23969f-21d6-59fa-ae3a-12250146c743" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)=1,\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x)=\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36689/selection/fbc9773ac823968caf88f84821376893dad8a149675d0331f444073366ee7364" :answer/id #uuid "2e8314ce-a943-5add-a8e6-be8a969fa8cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x)=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36689/selection/6d181db77dbc1c9591a703e2b0773992ba66bcb646499f1d8acc2a9f4be99cb3" :answer/id #uuid "762a6ab8-dd63-580d-b922-46761c15d5bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)=\\text{DNE},\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x)=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36689/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4860b19-76cc-5025-ac54-fb11d1481f30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36689/selection/ddedad0302f892b63bf1e984a158163f154d4d6538ed080f2a33dd117942102a" :answer-field/choices ["q-36689/selection/ddedad0302f892b63bf1e984a158163f154d4d6538ed080f2a33dd117942102a" "q-36689/selection/8f1878b9a3e2c6e1f6d2557dc5bc5895e8a9cdd0aa2e6ee51aee1e1dcbcc153a" "q-36689/selection/6e204d9b0a5fef6e7dd8e47841a025509ba9d4cebc253b0f618e32391fae7411" "q-36689/selection/fbc9773ac823968caf88f84821376893dad8a149675d0331f444073366ee7364" "q-36689/selection/6d181db77dbc1c9591a703e2b0773992ba66bcb646499f1d8acc2a9f4be99cb3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36689" :question/id #uuid "1c632534-5515-5827-b9ee-67d121a8015a" :question/math-academy-id "q-36689" :question/problem "Find the left- and right-sided limits at $x=0$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{-x}+1 & \\text{ for }\\,x<0 \\\\ {e}^{x} & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the left, we have $x<0,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\sqrt{-x}+1.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(\\sqrt{-x}+1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{-0}+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApproaching from the right, we have $x>0,$ so we use the expression $f(x)={e}^{x}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}{e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-36689/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0995bfd4-20b1-5f12-9d1d-fcb180a6291e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36689"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36702"] :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the left, we have $x<2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)={x}^{2}-x-2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}{x}^{2}-x-2 \\\\  & =(2)^{2}-2-2 \\\\  & =4-2-2 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36707"] :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the right, we have $x>2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}x \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-36724/selection/002bec980b6c5345ede7c9b7b54c1adb91f14dee9a4611d10d29f0c1e746b103" :answer/id #uuid "390bec18-e583-5fa1-bcc0-13d5ad2c6cd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36724/selection/0b237213ba3a5f9acb42f662821883129a5180451e3f2c065d788407a5a4279f" :answer/id #uuid "b9551551-e593-5800-8bcc-59d2098a3e01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36724/selection/718198356d72e4f94be2227397b7abab9b559940ca65e2af19277893fab4945b" :answer/id #uuid "6ab3f48c-bee3-5016-9a2b-8ab201cb770d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36724/selection/725623cb454beb2a68e890afae55af24b55803aa28eb83cd496fac30b8736604" :answer/id #uuid "5e9ecb6d-cfb8-5e87-bddd-6e44e77f6b39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36724/selection/dce6d2b99717fc0dab581f2a7b68ad0e371ea7e982b9c3be802e037eb7d3f221" :answer/id #uuid "8096a8e3-284f-5d79-8411-40ba3aac3e65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36724/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "af298a4f-2c6a-5364-b205-4cf2b8146e7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36724/selection/718198356d72e4f94be2227397b7abab9b559940ca65e2af19277893fab4945b" :answer-field/choices ["q-36724/selection/002bec980b6c5345ede7c9b7b54c1adb91f14dee9a4611d10d29f0c1e746b103" "q-36724/selection/0b237213ba3a5f9acb42f662821883129a5180451e3f2c065d788407a5a4279f" "q-36724/selection/718198356d72e4f94be2227397b7abab9b559940ca65e2af19277893fab4945b" "q-36724/selection/725623cb454beb2a68e890afae55af24b55803aa28eb83cd496fac30b8736604" "q-36724/selection/dce6d2b99717fc0dab581f2a7b68ad0e371ea7e982b9c3be802e037eb7d3f221"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36724" :question/id #uuid "788e4f94-c59e-54a9-87d5-7621f4a91cea" :question/math-academy-id "q-36724" :question/problem "Find the limit at $x=3$ for the function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{3x-1}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<3 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\pi )\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the left, we have $x<3,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{3x-1}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}\\sqrt[3]{3x-1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{3\\cdot 3-1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApproaching from the right, we have $x>3,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\pi ).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi ) \\\\  & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the two limits are different, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 3}f(x)=\\text{DNE}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-36724/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdd4a2e4-b0e6-54e8-972c-3dc194ce4ab3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36724"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339892/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1506879a-40a4-5588-92da-c27bcf122f21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339892/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "513a33ea-c554-5106-ba89-32723b991fae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339892/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-339892/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339892" :question/id #uuid "d540969a-8204-54d6-b275-8a37ed4ce9bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-339892" :question/problem "Find the right-sided limit at $x=8$ for the function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-3x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le 8 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{x}+2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {8}^{+}}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the right, we have $x>8,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}+2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {8}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {8}^{+}}(\\sqrt[3]{x}+2) \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{8}+2 \\\\  & =2+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339892/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdd4a2e4-b0e6-54e8-972c-3dc194ce4ab3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339892"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-37488/selection/66ce90f7bb453367423282bed905721336828a039136889438ab74215bdfadf7" :answer/id #uuid "8e286f49-4122-52df-aff2-2a3460380287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37488/selection/c31e47013924e0d920d694c2006358c753c8785db2b85b5a218a416b56e494d5" :answer/id #uuid "484114ef-32e4-514d-85f9-fe3452f2c29f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37488/selection/8004e7866d86c80ded47b2741a8aeae0f6b385d316409896da4460f3f2a0bde7" :answer/id #uuid "2e5d91ad-a490-594e-98e7-599620d66a45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)=\\text{DNE}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37488/selection/d00ba26d07c338bd26be465d5dc2aa5f32fae51cba1092cc61e010b80613c333" :answer/id #uuid "61db10cc-da85-527c-a90e-3e9220155ed6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37488/selection/d58e6c04953f8abe5d7ca1fabfd7b3a985b4f0ed54f06443ad190c503391f6e9" :answer/id #uuid "a8804906-47c5-51b5-93dc-75941a380720" :answer/typ