ve $x<-1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)={x}^{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}{x}^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, approaching $x=1$ from the right, we have $x>1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=3.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}3=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-99968/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bc794c7-cd0c-5ebc-aa11-9b82e72905fd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99968"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340040/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "46e8ca14-763b-5506-954f-eb3561049fb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340040/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f6afa44-4807-5dbb-8586-a1a918d4517b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340040/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-340040/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340040/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "81a5d834-2e20-5b4d-963a-94cc03176bd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340040/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a0c96fe-89a3-5834-ac24-3728fbd2f0a1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340040/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-340040/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340040" :question/id #uuid "3afc958b-0814-5f07-86e8-35c3521bb224" :question/math-academy-id "q-340040" :question/problem "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}a{x}^{2}+2x-3\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le 2 \\\\ 4x+b\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=9.$ Find the values of the constants $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "In order for ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ to be equal to $8,$ the left and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal to $8.$\n\n- Approaching from the left, we have $x\\le 2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=a{x}^{2}+2x-3.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}(a{x}^{2}+2x-3) \\\\  & =a({2}^{2})+2(2)-3 \\\\  & =4a+1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left-sided limit must be equal to $9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & =9 \\\\ 4a+1 & =9 \\\\ 4a & =8 \\\\ a & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Approaching from the right, we have $x>2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=4x+b.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}(4x+b) \\\\  & =4(2)+b \\\\  & =8+b\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the right-sided limit must be equal to $9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & =9 \\\\ 8+b & =9 \\\\ b & =9-8 \\\\ b & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340040/field-1" "q-340040/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4014376-4dae-56f1-b981-b35d3afab874"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340040"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340301/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "84ae7f5e-bf9b-512b-8be2-f1734af5a16e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340301/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b92db5cd-0671-5e46-9d45-b7a1dd7dda9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340301/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "50a635c6-0080-5232-986d-e9e04906e397" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340301/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-340301/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-340301/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340301" :question/id #uuid "b91dcbc6-c425-5994-85d5-426529628a2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-340301" :question/problem "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{\\,\\,sin(x-1)}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<1 \\\\ p{x}^{3}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=3.$ What is the value of the constant $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In order for ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)$ to be equal to $3,$ the left and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal to $3.$\n\n- Approaching from the left, we have $x<1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=3{e}^{\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)}.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}3{e}^{\\,\\,sin(x-1)} \\\\  & =3{e}^{\\,\\,sin(1-1)} \\\\  & =3{e}^{\\,\\,sin(0)} \\\\  & =3{e}^{0} \\\\  & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Approaching from the right, we have $x>1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=p{x}^{3}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(p{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =p\\cdot {1}^{3} \\\\  & =p\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the left and right-sided limits must be equal, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) \\\\ p & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-340301/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4014376-4dae-56f1-b981-b35d3afab874"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340301"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-302142/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "e6eb97f3-da1e-583f-9beb-b714c2d594e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-302142/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b55d56d-946c-5ba5-807c-4eecbe5277fe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-302142/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-302142/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-302142/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "911cc444-eb62-53f8-8e67-c3f3eed3ae36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-302142/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "da12a107-aa17-5bc1-b6e0-ec22b4a7f8b2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-302142/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-302142/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-302142" :question/id #uuid "94f1b338-29da-5fa4-8842-fa97970f2c94" :question/math-academy-id "q-302142" :question/problem "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}a{x}^{2}-3x+2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,-3\\le x<1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-bx\\, & \\text{ for }\\,1\\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=4.$ Find the values of the constants $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,$\n\n$b=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "In order for ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)$ to be equal to $4,$ the left and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal to $4.$\n\n- Approaching from the left, we have $-3\\le x<1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=a{x}^{2}-3x+2.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}(a{x}^{2}-3x+2) \\\\  & =a({1}^{2})-3(1)+2 \\\\  & =a-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left-sided limit must be equal to $4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & =4 \\\\ a-1 & =4 \\\\ a & =4+1 \\\\ a & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Approaching from the right, we have $1\\le x\\le 3,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-bx.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}(3{x}^{2}-bx) \\\\  & =3({1}^{2})-b(1) \\\\  & =3-b\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the right-sided limit must be equal to $4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & =4 \\\\ 3-b & =4 \\\\ b & =3-4 \\\\ b & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-302142/field-1" "q-302142/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4014376-4dae-56f1-b981-b35d3afab874"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-302142"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-99961/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0088c894-6d66-58d9-a277-1f166377306c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99961/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d9438753-96a1-520c-b7ef-053b52acf7cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99961/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "8f5f167b-39aa-5aa8-958c-fb5b97f70240" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99961/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "301ca70d-9d1e-5e85-ab1e-1861d2e619d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99961/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "de06d3a4-f52d-5112-842e-854d7528e11c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99961/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b254be2b-ffa7-5487-ae80-d26c76875486" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-99961/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-99961/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-99961/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-99961/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-99961/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-99961/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-99961" :question/id #uuid "864478b8-5b0e-578f-950b-2e87704cfe73" :question/math-academy-id "q-99961" :question/problem "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le -1 \\\\ x+c\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=1.$ What is the value of the constant $c?$" :question/worked-solution "In order for ${lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)$ to be equal to $1,$ the left and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal to $1.$\n\n- Approaching from the left, we have $x<-1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=-x.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}(-x) \\\\  & =-(-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Approaching from the right, we have $x>-1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=x+c.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}(x+c) \\\\  & =-1+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the left and right-sided limits must be equal, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x) \\\\ 1 & =-1+c \\\\ c & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-99961/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4014376-4dae-56f1-b981-b35d3afab874"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99961"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-36712/selection/2f8ad41f5722a1f34e7baafe29f44806af49e65dcc55adeddded970e1d59c04f" :answer/id #uuid "eb328d7b-ad8d-533c-bc71-f0c0da871646" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36712/selection/dba6bd026a0b165a39e6cc69c008e69f5308949bc1f1547907b185fa1b77f2d9" :answer/id #uuid "72c8747c-b211-5c74-8503-331dab0f0241" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36712/selection/48b22295c70c0ca7b0933ce12ad9e3474e27804d2784b222eb4949f4436a7340" :answer/id #uuid "ad775e72-87f7-54a1-91d0-d59a27a12e24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36712/selection/c6711f7ad55126457bd2e521873c7b1f6ee88809b4a9df461752e9c057710b51" :answer/id #uuid "7e60bf61-e857-5b0b-8df3-21f1fa5b18c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36712/selection/9649e01aa310fdf1bc1d3e47144acbfdc9c26cb2b376edc1d713070663055fbd" :answer/id #uuid "b348ba9d-a7ad-5471-ba58-11703cd47f9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "c=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36712/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "277453aa-cef8-5ae2-aa8d-700d172e8830" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36712/selection/9649e01aa310fdf1bc1d3e47144acbfdc9c26cb2b376edc1d713070663055fbd" :answer-field/choices ["q-36712/selection/2f8ad41f5722a1f34e7baafe29f44806af49e65dcc55adeddded970e1d59c04f" "q-36712/selection/dba6bd026a0b165a39e6cc69c008e69f5308949bc1f1547907b185fa1b77f2d9" "q-36712/selection/48b22295c70c0ca7b0933ce12ad9e3474e27804d2784b222eb4949f4436a7340" "q-36712/selection/c6711f7ad55126457bd2e521873c7b1f6ee88809b4a9df461752e9c057710b51" "q-36712/selection/9649e01aa310fdf1bc1d3e47144acbfdc9c26cb2b376edc1d713070663055fbd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36712" :question/id #uuid "c8e54158-9b0b-5467-b616-e74e1922dae9" :question/math-academy-id "q-36712" :question/problem "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<2 \\\\ c\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=2.$ What is the value of the constant $c?$" :question/worked-solution "In order for ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ to be equal to $2,$ the left and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal to $2.$\n\n- Approaching from the left, we have $x<2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=x.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}x \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Approaching from the right, we have $x>2,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=c.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}c \\\\  & =c\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the left and right-sided limits must be equal, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x) \\\\ c & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-36712/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4014376-4dae-56f1-b981-b35d3afab874"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36712"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
